<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello. <br>During the operation of the new version, I noticed very rare decoding failures and modulation failures. This happened with a long monologue and, possibly, loud modulation from the interlocutor.</div></blockquote>Decoding failures are quite common on DMR, it is not necessarily a problem with the firmware.</div></blockquote>This is not a global DMR failure. At the control station (Anytone D878UV), reception was not interrupted, on rt3s, at the moment of sound loss, the LED showed the presence of reception, S-metr showed a high level of the received signal. Such errors have become much rarer, but they are there.</div></blockquote>Comparisons of the radio to other DMR radios is not valid. <br><br>The Anytone radios do not use the same hardware, and have much bettery noise immunity.<br><br>DMR decode failure does not necessarilty mean a problem with the firmware.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Oct 09, 2022 9:43 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
