		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2409&amp;p=19975#p19975"><![CDATA[
A new Alpha version is now available<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MDUV380/Firmware/745233bd3320a5d9a528a3f453998e72437be456" class="postlink">downloads/MDUV380/Firmware/745233bd3320 ... 72437be456</a><br><br>The following things should be fixed<br><br>* DMR Rx dropout<br>* DTMF transmit from contacts list<br><br>This version also has better power saving on Eco modes greater than 1.<br><br>Note.<br>The changes to the power saving have an effect on when the USB can be connected to the radio.<br>Please turn off the radio before connecting the USB cable. The turn the radio on again, and the USB and CPS should work OK.<br><br>BTW.<br><br>I've noticed the USB hardware on these radios seems to suffer from RFI pickup on the USB cable.<br>For example, if I turn on a flourescent lamp in my shack, I hear my PC beep to indicate a USB device has disconnected and then reconnected.<br><br>This was happening even before the power saving changes, so I think the USB hardware in these radio seems to be less robust than in the GD77, or the MD9600<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Oct 03, 2022 4:13 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
